part places
  tally 1
  note "Places of household B. Accounts open with no opening row: their balances are holes until an anchor (a stated balance from an export, L §5.18), which the record files give. Outside places name where money comes from and goes."

place cis: account DUK

place savings: account DUK

place b_lazur: account FLR

place wrzos: account DUK

place mortgage: debt DUK

place clients_owe: claim DUK

place kessel_owes: claim FLR

place bartek: claim DUK

place clients: outside DUK

place revenue_office: outside DUK

place b_sio: outside DUK

place jodla: outside DUK

place bank_cis: outside DUK

place mewa: outside DUK

place association: outside DUK

place insurer: outside DUK

input cisr[r in cis_row]: movement DUK (kind key row_kind)

input sav[r in sav_row]: movement DUK

input laz[r in laz_row]: movement FLR (inv key inv_flr)

input wrz[r in wrz_row]: movement DUK

place elsewhere: outside DUK

place elsewhere_flr: outside FLR

version b_openings
  cite b_modeller
  known 2022-03-01
  note "Every place opens empty on the model's first day: the claims (no invoice before the business, B-D01; the loan to Bartek is made 2025-02-10, B-D24), the floren account (opened 2025-01-02, B-D23), the mortgage (paid out on the deed's day, B-D07 .1). The accounts' real balances come from the exports' anchors (stated), which re-anchor them; before an account's first anchor its balance is the model's, not the bank's."
  note "E1 copy (O:E1-3): B's row opening[*] = 0 is restated for each place B declares with no key, the keys the built-in index place had on 2022-03-01 in B alone, because a * row covers the keys its index has on its known date (L §6.2) and in the family that index also holds the places of A and D, whose openings are their own or missing on purpose (A's joint account, D's konto)."
  opening[cis] = 0 assumed "no balance is known before the first export's anchor; 0 keeps the claims and the debt exact" "modeller"
  opening[savings] = 0 assumed "no balance is known before the first export's anchor; 0 keeps the claims and the debt exact" "modeller"
